  "notes": "{刷|す}り{込|こ}む has psychological and physical meanings.\n\nSENSE 1 - PSYCHOLOGICAL:\n- {刷|す}り{込|こ}み: imprinting (psychology term)\n- {価値観|かちかん}を{刷|す}り{込|こ}む: to instill values\n- {刷|す}り{込|こ}まれる: to be conditioned/imprinted\n\nIMPRINTING (psychology):\nThe term {刷|す}り{込|こ}み is used in Japanese psychology for \"imprinting,\" the phenomenon where young animals form attachments during critical periods.\n\nSENSE 2 - PHYSICAL:\n- クリームを{刷|す}り{込|こ}む: to rub in cream\n- {調味料|ちょうみりょう}を{刷|す}り{込|こ}む: to rub in seasonings",
